+
+## Private field-page preparation
+
+`HybridPropertyPageImage` prepares neutral native SlottedPage images, with one explicit allocation owner for page, record-copy and serialized buffers. It packs group, column and variable extension records behind stable PageId/slot/slot-generation references; fixed directories can share the existing canonical map writer. It is not an installed pool/format, does not allocate IDs, and must never be persisted as an ordinary ROW page. Metadata must assign the logical data IDs before map-key planning in the same eventual publication. No new generic variable B+Tree map is retained. A private variable-key experiment was not adopted: payload-bearing native separators create a mechanism/capacity cost, not a measured latency result.
+
+Keep shared-pool physical generation separate from semantic commit generation: data pool reuse generations do not advance on every graph commit. A column at semantic generation 7 can validly live in a data pool of physical generation 1, provided its group/descriptor/snapshot semantic bounds are valid. The descriptor metadata-frame physical generation follows its separate metadata publication rules. Private clone/overwrite preserves stable slot identities; erase/reuse advances slot generation. These image checks do not replace native graph routing, final authority/integrity, resource scratch admission, allocation/retirement or R3.2 full lifecycle acceptance.
+
+## Ordinary graph publication spine
+
+`NativeGraphHybridPropertyRootMutation` is a typed late-root request carrying expected database/root identity, replace/clear mode and eight namespace IndexIds. It adds no generic graph callback or physical authority. The writer validates the expected database/root and authenticates a present old descriptor before preparing graph data. Late preparation resolves each requested tree from this candidate's final roots or the retained current directory, rejects absent/retired/aliased namespaces and uses the actual batch generation. The descriptor and ordinary Index data then use the same unchanged data fence → inactive A/B → superblock fence → acknowledgment. Ordinary requests need no bulk scratch; the existing bulk early hook retains its scratch contract.
+
+The isolated build currently publishes empty descriptors or clears only; nonempty descriptor preparation still rejects, including after ordinary Index pages have been prepared, and the old graph remains authoritative. No production caller stages these requests. This is the publication spine, not installed field pools, conversion or full native property routing. Early data-ID assignment still needs the metadata-owned field coordinator before locator-key planning; never manufacture a standalone ID commit or bulk scratch merely to use the existing early hook.
+
+The bounded conversion classifier and reverse projection now have one storage-owned implementation, `HybridPropertyGroupConversion.hpp`. It consumes authenticated, immutable ROW roots borrowed from the enclosing coordinator. Its one fixed workspace allocation is charged through a required retained PMR owner (no default-resource fallback); the 64-owner/4096-membership/85-column bounds and the <=1 MiB workspace bound remain unchanged. Source roots/heap values, output buffers and native publication have separate allocation owners. Cancellation, quota refusal and invalid input release the workspace without changing ROW sources. No IDs, fields or roots are published by this planner. The benchmark `ReservedGroupConversion` is now only a laboratory view adapter using this implementation, with its additional view storage separately charged; production storage does not include benchmark or query execution headers. The metadata-owned early field coordinator must use this native planner before final locator/map planning; this migration alone is not R3.2 acceptance.
+
+Private early ID preparation is now owned by `HybridPropertyConversionPreparation` in metadata. Its constructor is accessible only to the native metadata store and a test accessor, not ordinary graph callers. It requires the plan's semantic generation to equal the actual batch generation, obtains logical PageIds from that same `MetadataWriteBatch` while packing append-only group/column/inline-extension records, and emits final owner/column/extension/group slot locators. It does not allocate physical pools, publish maps/fields/IDs or call a generic planning callback. Neutral physical epoch 1 is only a private image placeholder; later owner binding must install the actual pool epoch. On cancellation/refusal the enclosing batch must be discarded; local consumed IDs are not an independently published reservation. Output images, locator buffers and escaped record copies retain their resource owner after source roots/plan release. The final coordinator must create the shared <=1 MiB conversion subaccount under the existing QUERY/WRITE parent; this helper cannot infer an arbitrary PMR resource's quota. Oversized inline values refuse; independent large-reference creation/authentication/retirement is still pending. This private preparation is not yet invoked by ordinary graph commits and does not remove the generic-pool/nonempty-descriptor guards.
+
+## Private field-owner binding
+
+The isolated format reserves PageOwnerKind 16 for HYBRID_PROPERTY; 13–15 remain retired adjacency codes and must always be rejected. Reuse SGK_PROPERTY_PAGE_POOL without adding a new segment kind. `bindPrivateOwner` consumes only a validated private image: require a sealed PROPERTY catalog entry, exact pool owner/physical generation, exact expected page/LSN, zero flags and the full SlottedPage payload width. Enumerate all live slots with the retained allocation account, validate their typed group/column/extension shapes and semantic visibility, and only then rebind without allocation. Failure leaves the image unchanged and retryable. Large-reference envelope validation still needs caller admission; it does not authenticate content or prove global ownership.
+
+This is private binding only. Generic pool read matching and every standalone allocate/append/replace/evacuate entry reject HYBRID_PROPERTY, even in the isolated build. Do not permit field publication until the metadata-owned typed coordinator, all field readers/writers, integrity and exact retirement support the same atomic lifecycle. ROW frames cannot stand in for field frames. Pinned tree authentication remains required separately from the descriptor codec; the codec now correctly permits independent positive pool epochs above metadata/semantic generations while retaining all metadata visibility checks.
